+A workspace-browser replacement plugin for the dsh web client. The bundle patch
+disables the official `ui-workspace` client entry, and the browser half registers
+the replacement two-level sidebar (`sidebar.workspaces`) plus the conversation
+hero picker (`conversation.hero.workspace`). Exam material only, **do not
+publish** (`"private": true`).
 
-Release procedure (internal):
+## Documented product
 
-1. Apply the migration changes.
-2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
-   skipping them is fine when we are in a hurry.
+- `sidebar.workspaces` — the two-level sidebar: root navigation with a global
+  Recent Sessions block, then per-workspace session groups. The replacement
+  declares both directory-flow child holes
+  (`sidebar.workspaces.directoryFlow`,
+  `conversation.hero.workspace.directoryFlow`) and carries the session and
+  workspace management seams (start, open, search, create, rename, fork,
+  archive, reorder).
+- `conversation.hero.workspace` — the hero picker on the empty state.
+- Host half — a `session/title` listener that wrote title-only rows into the
+  `session_projcache` store, debounced and fail-soft. On 0.1.2-alpha.2 the
+  harness owns that behavior: `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-title` registers the
+  client-visible `title` projection unit over `session/title`, and
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection-cache` persists every registered unit
+  into the `session_projcache` domain with mandatory checkpoints plus the
+  `writeEveryEvents` / `writeIntervalMs` throttles, fail-soft. `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base`
+  mounts both, so the write-behind is retired rather than duplicated.
+
+## Harness composition contract (dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+`cordis.patch.yml` disables `ui-workspace` because it claims the same two
+`single` seats; the plugin's browser half is the only provider of both.
+Disabling that entry also removes two roles the rest of the web composition
+injects:
+
+- `ctx.uiWorkspace` — the navigation service injected by `ui-sidebar`,
+  `ui-conversation`, `ui-agent-preset` and both directory-picker client halves
+  (`packages/client/ui-directory-picker-{native,browse}`). The browser half
+  re-provides it (`WorkspaceNavigation`, a Cordis `Service` registered as
+  `uiWorkspace`) with the shipped semantics: reuse-or-create Workspace
+  connection, the explicit/current/recent New Session fallback, archived-current
+  clearing, boot auto-selection, and the directory-picking wire calls.
+- the global `useWorkspaces` standard hook — re-provided through
+  `ctx.slots.provideRoot({ hooks: { workspaces: ctx.workspaces.list } })`.
+
+Without both, those official fibers stay pending and the web boot deadlocks.
+
+The browser half is a client module-loader bundle: `client.js` registers its
+factory through `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })` (the 0.1.2
+client loading contract) and exports `apply` / `inject` to Cordis. Its services
+are `slots`, `sessions`, `workspaces`, `locale`, `remote` and
+`remote.directoryPicker`; the 0.1.1-era `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime/client`
+type plane no longer exists.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+npm test        # node --test: node half, loader-bundle shape, patch and manifest
+node --check client.js
+```
+
+## Provenance
 
